From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: fall back to pkg-config for SDL2

Some distributions, including openEuler 24.03 LTS SP3, provide SDL2 headers,
libraries, and sdl2.pc without an SDL2 CMake package configuration. Use the
standard pkg-config metadata when find_package(SDL2) cannot expose an imported
SDL2 target, including when CMake's legacy FindSDL2 module reports success with
variables only. Expose every imported target expected by the rest of the build.

The empty SDL2main interface is intentional on Unix, where the main wrapper is
not required. No bundled SDL copy is fetched.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of raptor 0.8.1 CMakeLists.txt
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,7 +41,15 @@ elseif(WIN32)
     find_package(SDL2 REQUIRED)
     include_directories(${SDL2_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 else()
-    find_package(SDL2 REQUIRED)
+    find_package(SDL2 QUIET)
+    if(NOT TARGET SDL2::SDL2)
+        find_package(PkgConfig REQUIRED)
+        pkg_check_modules(SDL2 REQUIRED IMPORTED_TARGET sdl2)
+        add_library(SDL2::SDL2 ALIAS PkgConfig::SDL2)
+    endif()
+    if(NOT TARGET SDL2::SDL2main)
+        add_library(SDL2::SDL2main INTERFACE IMPORTED)
+    endif()
     include_directories(${SDL2_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 endif()
 
